E["subzone:valley-of-bones"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Bones",z="shendralas",s="The Valley of Bones is a desolate canyon along the crags of Shen'dralas, choked with dust, ancient remains, and restless undead. Haunted by the lingering spirits of the Magram centaur clan and patrolled by dark necromancers, it is dominated by the colossal rib cages of mysterious ancient beasts known as the Dead Goliaths.",h="The Valley of Bones is a desolate canyon along the crags of Shen'dralas, choked with dust, ancient remains...",sec={{t="A Canyon of the Restless Dead",b="Tucked away in the southern reaches of the region, the Valley of Bones lives up to its grim name. Skeletal horrors walk the dusty ravines, raised and bound by centaur necromancers who draw upon dark sorceries. The spirits of deceased Magram centaur wander the wastes alongside them, bound to this barren earth long after their violent deaths. Adding to the canyon's ominous nature are the Dead Goliaths—two immense skeletons slumped against the rocky cliffs whose true origin remains a total mystery to scholars and wanderers alike.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Dead Goliaths?",a="The Dead Goliaths are the colossal remains of two massive, unidentified creatures resting against the canyon walls. Little is known about what species they belonged to or when they died, though their sheer scale suggests beasts from an ancient, forgotten era.",al={"giant bones","huge skeletons desolace","dead goliaths lore"}},{q="Why are there centaur ghosts here?",a="The spirits belong to the Magram clan, one of the violent centaur tribes native to these arid plains. Between the unending inter-clan warfare and the presence of centaur necromancers meddling with the dead, their spirits have been denied rest, haunting the canyon as wandering apparitions.",al={"magram ghosts","why centaur spirits","undead centaur"}},{q="Who controls the skeletons in the valley?",a="Centaur necromancers practice dark rites within the canyon, raising and commanding skeletal minions to guard the crags and maintain their foothold among the dead.",al={"who commands skeletons","necromancers valley of bones"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="The desecration of spirits in the valley is severe, as dark practitioners pervert the natural transition of death by binding Magram souls and raising twisted skeletal servitors."},kw={"centaur","dead goliaths","magram","necromancers","shen'dralas","skeletons","valley of bones"},rel={"zone:shendralas","zone:desolace","topic:centaur"},src={"Valley of Bones"}}
E["zone:shendralas"] = {t="zone",n="Shen'dralas",z="shendralas",s="Shen'dralas is a rugged, contested wilderness situated between Feralas, Mulgore, and south-eastern Desolace. Dominated by ancient night elven remnants and troubled borders, it serves as a volatile crossroads where encroaching centaur, displaced outcasts, and bristling quilboar collide.",h="Shen'dralas is a rugged, contested wilderness situated between Feralas, Mulgore, and south-eastern Desolace.",sec={{t="A Borderland in Turmoil",b="Tucked away in the heights south-east of Desolace and bordered by Mulgore and Feralas, Shen'dralas is a raw borderland far removed from major faction capitols. Its craggy passes and hidden enclaves harbor desperate groups carving out existence on the edge of wild Kalimdor. From secluded vantage points like Evenshade Overlook to lawless refuges like Outcast Hideaway, the zone is defined by those who wish to watch unseen or stay forgotten.",sp=0},{t="Centaur, Quilboar, and Ancient Ruins",b="The land bears the distinct mark of the highborne legacy that gave it its name, yet it is far from peaceful. Centaur conflict bleeds across the Magram Front, keeping old blood feuds alive and well along its borders. Meanwhile, encroaching quilboar maintain fortified redoubts such as Bristleback Retreat, turning every shadowed ravine into contested territory for any traveler passing through.",sp=0},{t="The Valley of Bones",b="Leading out toward north-western Desolace lies the Valley of Bones, a grim corridor that serves as the primary overland access route into Shen'dralas. Bleached by sun and wind, this passage stands as a harsh reminder of the violent struggles that constantly ripple through these crags.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Shen'dralas located?",a="Shen'dralas lies south-east of Desolace, nestled between the borders of Feralas and Mulgore. Travelers arriving on foot typically enter from Desolace by passing through the Valley of Bones.",al={"where is shendralas","shendralas location","how to get to shendralas"}},{q="Is Shen'dralas controlled by the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Neither faction holds dominion here. Shen'dralas is a contested frontier populated by roving centaur, hostile quilboar, outcasts, and isolated encampments.",al={"is shendralas horde","is shendralas alliance","who owns shendralas"}},{q="What major settlements or landmarks are here?",a="Prominent landmarks include the Valley of Bones, Bristleback Retreat, Evenshade Overlook, the Magram Front, Outcast Hideaway, and the central expanse of Shen'dralas itself.",al={"shendralas subzones","landmarks in shendralas","points of interest shendralas"}},{q="Why are there centaur here?",a="Centaur territorial wars extend from the plains of Desolace straight into the region along the Magram Front, where the clan clashes against local defenders and rival factions.",al={"centaur in shendralas","magram front","why are magram here"}},{q="What is Bristleback Retreat?",a="Bristleback Retreat is a fortified outpost held by Bristleback quilboar who have established a fierce foothold along the edges of the zone.",al={"bristleback retreat","quilboar in shendralas"}},{q="What is the connection between this zone and Lake Dumont?",a="Geographically, the wilderness of Shen'dralas sits across the mountainous territory where the secluded Lake Dumont sits tucked away in old survey charts.",al={"lake dumont","shendralas map history"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The name evokes the ancient Highborne lore of Eldre'Thalas, drawing the attention of sentinels wary of reckless arcana in southern Kalimdor.",["race:Tauren"]="With the region bordering Mulgore and Desolace, the aggression of quilboar and centaur along these ridges poses a direct threat to nearby ancestral hunting grounds.",["faction:Alliance"]="A remote, contested wilderness providing alternate routes between Feralas and central Kalimdor, fraught with dangers that require keen vigilance.",["faction:Horde"]="Positioned just outside the southern reaches of Mulgore, keeping the Magram and quilboar contained here is vital for protecting Horde frontiers."},kw={"bristleback retreat","desolace","evenshade overlook","feralas","lake dumont","magram front","mulgore","outcast hideaway","shendralas","valley of bones"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-bones","zone:desolace","zone:feralas","zone:mulgore","subzone:lake-dumont"},src={"Shen'dralas"}}
